### User Management API Tests
### Base URL: http://localhost:8080

### 1. Get all users (should return empty list initially)
GET http://localhost:8080/users
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Create a new user
POST http://localhost:8080/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "telephone": "+1-555-0123",
  "address": {
    "street": "123 Main St",
    "city": "New York",
    "state": "NY",
    "zip": "10001",
    "country": "United States",
    "countryCode": "US"
  }
}

###get user by email and password
GET http://localhost:8080/users/loginPasswordEncoded/penni.welch@hotmail.com/password123
Accept: application/json

### 3. Create another user
POST http://localhost:8080/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "JosephQuan ",
  "email": "josepheducationplatform@gmail.com",
  "telephone": "+32496784139",
  "password": "password123",
  "address": {
    "street": "Minister Delbekelaan 33",  
    "city": "Antwerp",
    "state": "Antwerp",
    "zip": "2170",
    "country": "Belgium",
    "countryCode": "BE"
  },
  "profile": {
    "firstName": "Joseph",
    "lastName": "Quansah Kotei",
    "avatar": "https://media.tenor.com/hD5dujWbbq0AAAAm/really-zhao.webp",
    "preferences": {
      "language": "English",
      "theme": "dark",
      "notifications": true
    }
},
    "role": "USER"
}

###

### 4. Get all users (should now return the created users)
GET http://localhost:8080/users/all
Accept: application/json

###

### 5. Get user by ID (replace with actual UUID from previous responses)
# Note: Replace the UUID below with an actual ID from the GET all users response
GET http://localhost:8080/users/f80d7deb-b8b7-415c-b977-c1239641e24d
Accept: application/json

###

### 5.1 Remove user by Id
# Note: Replace the UUID below with an actual ID from the GET all users response
DELETE http://localhost:8080/users/f80d7deb-b8b7-415c-b977-c1239641e24d
Accept: application/json

###

### 6. Update user (replace with actual UUID and modify the user data)
# Note: Replace the UUID below with an actual ID from the GET all users response
PUT http://localhost:8080/users/3a993f72-f58d-402d-9aaa-3bac0ebe3fed
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "3a993f72-f58d-402d-9aaa-3bac0ebe3fed",
  "name": "John Doe Updated",
  "email": "john.doe.updated@example.com",
  "telephone": "+1-555-9999",
  "address": {
    "street": "789 Updated St",
    "city": "Updated City",
    "state": "UC",
    "zip": "99999",
    "country": "United States",
    "countryCode": "US"
  }
}

###

### 7. Delete user by ID (replace with actual UUID)
# Note: Replace the UUID below with an actual ID from the GET all users response
DELETE http://localhost:8080/users/4dee8edb-d401-4c08-b332-ecbecb14b214

###

### 8. Verify user was deleted - Get all users again
GET http://localhost:8080/users
Accept: application/json

###

### 9. Test error case - Get non-existent user
GET http://localhost:8080/users/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Accept: application/json

###

### 10. Test error case - Create user with null data
POST http://localhost:8080/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": null,
  "email": null,
  "telephone": null,
  "address": null
}

###

### 11. Test minimal user creation (only required fields)
POST http://localhost:8080/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Minimal User",
  "email": "minimal@example.com"
}

###

### Instructions:
### 1. Start your Spring Boot application first: ./gradlew bootRun
### 2. Execute these requests in order
### 3. Copy actual UUIDs from responses to replace the placeholder UUIDs in requests 5, 6, and 7
### 4. The application uses an in-memory database, so data will be lost when you restart the app
